# Force-resident denylist for tools/find-init-candidates.py.
#
# Functions here are NEVER placed in the discardable INIT section, even when
# they look statically init-only.  They are runtime-installed driver entry
# points -- IRP dispatch routines, AddDevice, video/SMBus bring-up helpers --
# reachable from code that runs (or whose function pointer can be invoked)
# after MiFreeInitializationCode discards INIT.  For dispatch handlers the
# address is written into a long-lived resident DRIVER_OBJECT/DEVICE_OBJECT at
# boot; that store is invisible to static analysis, so discarding the handler
# would be a latent use-after-free (e.g. a DVD media-change PnP IRP dispatched
# to a freed handler).  The safety call is therefore explicit here rather than
# inferred.
#
# Denying a function also keeps its whole reachable callee set resident: the
# closure only moves a callee when every caller is INIT or chosen, and a denied
# caller is never chosen.  So this list only needs the roots that static
# analysis can't see are runtime-reachable; the rest fall out automatically.
# (find-init-candidates.py only places functions -- discardable *data* is governed
# by DATA_SEG("INITDATA") tags in the source, not this list.)
#
# Base names: no leading _/@, no @N / .constprop / .lto_priv suffix.

# --- Storage / PCI-IDE driver entry points (installed into DRIVER_OBJECTs) ---
AtaAddChannel
AtaDispatchPnp
CdromAddDevice
ClassAddDevice
ClassDispatchPnp
DiskAddDevice
PartMgrPnp
PciIdeXAddDevice
PciIdeXDispatchPnp
PciPnpControl

# --- Video / SMBus bring-up helpers reachable from resident display code ---
I2CTransmitByteGetReturn
I2CTransmitWord
I2CWriteBytetoRegister
ReadfromSMBus
WriteToSMBus
xbv_malloc
